WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.369
JAMIE: Yesterday Rufus was observing
that the market is betting on speed
while

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:06.739
JAMIE: offloading liability. Today's
Manus story is that same bet at the
company

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:10.108
JAMIE: level.

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:14.085
RUFUS: I'll accept that. Though I'd add:
the fact that investors paid a

00:00:14.085 --> 00:00:17.952
RUFUS: premium over the blocked
acquisition price is evidence that
independent Chinese AI

00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:21.818
RUFUS: infrastructure has a market value
that geopolitical friction hasn't
destroyed. That's an

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:25.685
RUFUS: interesting data point regardless
of what you think of it.

00:00:25.865 --> 00:00:29.493
ALEX: So the honest answer to the title
question: yes, they can survive

00:00:29.493 --> 00:00:33.122
ALEX: — Manus is proof of that — but the
regulatory risk doesn't

00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:36.750
ALEX: disappear when the acquisition
does. It follows the company.

00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:38.704
RUFUS: At a four-billion-dollar
valuation.
